cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cited as a reference for layer taxonomy only. No weights from this project are used."
title: "See-Through: layered decomposition of illustration"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Shitagaki Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/shitagaki-lab/see-through"
license: Apache-2.0
notes: "REFERENCE ONLY, and the distinction is the licence. The Apache-2.0 above covers
  the repository's code, which is what the taxonomy is read from --
  common/live2d/scrap_model.py, whose VALID_BODY_PARTS_V3 names 23 parts including the
  front hair / back hair and irides / eyewhite / eyelash / eyebrow splits.
  NO CHECKPOINT FROM THIS PROJECT IS USED. Every one the inference scripts load states no
  licence (layerdifforg/seethroughv0.0.1_marigold, 24yearsold/l2d_sam_iter2,
  24yearsold/seethroughv0.0.2_layerdiff3d_nf4) or is unreadable
  (24yearsold/metricdepth3d_tmp, HTTP 401). The depth checkpoint is further a fine-tune of
  prs-eth/marigold-depth-v1-1, CreativeML Open RAIL++-M over stable-diffusion-2, whose use
  restrictions travel into derivatives."
